WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.435
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.903
We hope you're doing well
tonight.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.005
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:09.776
Tomorrow is election day,
which means President Biden's

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.779
impeachment trial, I guess,
starts on Wednesday.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.614
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.783
Former president Trump
is reportedly planning

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.118
to formally announce
his presidential campaign

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.386
on November 14th.

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.889
No word yet on his choice
for V.P.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.591
or First Lady.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.527
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.662
Former President Barack Obama
and Donald Trump

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.365
held separate rallies over
the weekend in Pennsylvania.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.267
Obama campaigned
for John Fetterman,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.503
and Trump campaigned
for 2024.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:37.903
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:40.239
Democratic Congressional
Campaign Committee Chair

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.776
Sean Patrick Maloney said
in an interview yesterday

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:45.177
that Democrats will maintain
control of Congress and added,

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:48.414
quote, "We're not perfect,
but we are responsible adults

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:49.949
who didn't attack the Capitol."

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.752
Not exactly a high bar.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.086
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:56.890
Democrats are like the stepdad
of political parties.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.224
They may be lame,
but at least they're not the guy

00:00:59.224 --> 00:01:00.493
who walked out on you.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.561
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.264
"Hey, I'm here!"

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.566
Yesterday was the end of
daylight savings time,

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.968
in case you were wondering
why these all feel

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.838
more like 1:30 in the morning
jokes.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.640
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.408
The New York City marathon
was held yesterday,

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:19.812
and Kenyan runner Evans Chebet
was the men's champion

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:26.118
with a time of 2 hours,
8 minutes, and 41 seconds.

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:28.354
2 hours, 8 minutes,
and 41 seconds --

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:31.558
the fastest anyone has ever
gotten from Staten Island

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.926
to Central Park.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.828
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.997
At a rally in Pennsylvania
over the weekend,

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.099
former president Trump
called Florida governor

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:43.769
Ron DeSantis, quote,
"Ron DeSanctimonious."

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:48.208
Has anyone ever been worse at
coming up with nicknames?

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.709
Imagine Trump in "Top Gun."

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.478
People, people,
I know we all love Maverick,

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.046
but I think I got one
that beats it.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.114
Are you ready?
Everybody ready?

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.418
"Airplane Guy."

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.052
That's right,
former president Trump

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:01.854
referred to Florida governor
Ron DeSantis

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.657
as Ron DeSanctimonious,
which is a risky move for Trump

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.526
because that's six syllables.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.828
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:12.231
A J.C. Penney location in
Pennsylvania temporarily closed

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.834
last week after a deer wandered
into the store.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:18.438
Even crazier, a couple weeks
ago, a shopper wandered in.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:21.374
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:28.380
He's asking what aisle
stuff's in.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.816
Over 50 students in El Paso,
Texas,

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:32.418
may have to retake the S.A.T.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.087
after their answer sheets
flew out of a UPS truck

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:37.490
and were either lost
or destroyed.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.858
The students are calling
the incident disheartening,

00:02:39.858 --> 00:02:42.762
regrettable, disconcerting,
or irksome.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:46.933
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.034
Astronomers predict that
a total lunar eclipse

00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:50.303
will occur tomorrow.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.305
So, if you look outside
and the moon turns red,

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.908
Don't worry, it just means
Dr. Oz won his Senate race.

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:59.545
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.814
That's what the prophecy
foretold.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.717
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.353
And finally, the makers of
Miller Lite this week

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.655
will offer a Christmas tree
keg stand.

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.657
And if you're wondering
what Santa's bringing you --

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:13.226
AA pamphlets.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.229
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

